---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Laravel PDF Testing: test the PDF your app generates';
const description = 'Free, MIT-licensed PDF assertions for Pest and PHPUnit. Check the text, count the pages and compare rendered snapshots.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
<!--
  LAUNCH CHECKLIST (remove when done):
  1. TODO-DEMO: point the demo button (id="demo-todo") at the public demo repository URL.
  2. TODO-PACKAGIST: the page is written as already published; publish craigsimps/laravel-pdf-testing before go-live.
  3. TODO-ANALYTICS: optional, free and privacy-friendly only. A GoatCounter snippet is included at the
     end of the body, commented out. Leave it disabled until Craig decides.
  Copy for this page lives in this file only. Styling is in styles.css.
  The invoice pages in the hero are drawn in HTML; the numbers in them are sample data, not measurements.
-->
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

<header class="site-header on-ground">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Laravel PDF Testing, top of page">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path class="page" d="M8 3h12l6 6v18a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H8a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path class="page" d="M20 3v6h6" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path class="page" d="M11 14h7M11 18h10" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <path class="tick" d="M11 24l3 3 6-6" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
      Laravel PDF Testing
    </a>
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Page sections">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#checks">What it checks</a></li>
        <li><a href="#install">Install</a></li>
        <li><a href="#demo">Demo</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/craigsimps/laravel-pdf-testing">GitHub</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main id="main">
  <section class="hero on-ground" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Free · MIT · Composer dev package for Pest and PHPUnit</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Your PDF fake passed. Is the invoice total there?</h1>
        <p class="lead">Check the PDF your Laravel app generates. Assert that the invoice contains the right total, or compare its layout with an approved snapshot. A fake checks that you requested a PDF. These assertions check the resulting document.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#install">Install</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="#moment">See a failing test</a>
        </div>
        <p class="muted">Pass a Laravel test response, a file path or raw PDF bytes. Spatie Laravel PDF and Dompdf objects work too. No browser or hosted service required.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="snapshot crop" aria-labelledby="snap-caption">
        <div class="snap-row" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of three versions of the same invoice page: the approved baseline with a total of 120.00, this run with the total missing, and the diff image, in which the missing total is marked in red.">
          <div class="snap">
            <span class="snap-label">page-1.png<small>baseline</small></span>
            <div class="sheet" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="sheet-head"><span>Invoice 1001</span><span>Acme Ltd</span></div>
              <div class="bar w60"></div>
              <div class="bar w45"></div>
              <div class="row"><div class="bar"></div><span>100.00</span></div>
              <div class="row"><div class="bar"></div><span>20.00</span></div>
              <div class="total"><span>Total</span><span>120.00</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="snap">
            <span class="snap-label">actual-1.png<small>this run</small></span>
            <div class="sheet" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="sheet-head"><span>Invoice 1001</span><span>Acme Ltd</span></div>
              <div class="bar w60"></div>
              <div class="bar w45"></div>
              <div class="row"><div class="bar"></div><span>100.00</span></div>
              <div class="row"><div class="bar"></div><span>20.00</span></div>
              <div class="total is-missing"><span>Total</span><span>120.00</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="snap">
            <span class="snap-label is-diff">diff-1.png<small>312 changed pixels</small></span>
            <div class="sheet is-diff" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="sheet-head"><span>Invoice 1001</span><span>Acme Ltd</span></div>
              <div class="bar w60"></div>
              <div class="bar w45"></div>
              <div class="row"><div class="bar"></div><span>100.00</span></div>
              <div class="row"><div class="bar"></div><span>20.00</span></div>
              <div class="total"><span>Total</span><span>120.00</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="snap-caption" class="snap-msg"><span class="fail">⨯</span> <span class="dim">toMatchPdfSnapshot</span> PDF snapshot page 1: 312 changed pixels (allowed 0). Diff: tests/pdf-snapshots/invoice-1001/artifacts/diff-1.png</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="moment" id="moment" aria-labelledby="moment-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="titled" id="moment-title">What happens when the total goes missing</h2>
      <p>These three Pest tests check an invoice route. In this example, the total is missing: the text check shows what was extracted, and the snapshot check points to the diff. The figures shown are illustrative.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="split">
      <div class="pane pane-code">
        <div class="pane-inner">
          <p class="pane-title">tests/Feature/InvoicePdfTest.php</p>
          <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Pest test file"><code><span class="k">it</span>(<span class="s">'has one page'</span>, <span class="k">function</span> () &#123;
    <span class="k">expect</span>($this-&gt;get(<span class="s">'/invoices/1001/pdf'</span>))
        -&gt;toHavePdfPageCount(1);
&#125;);

<span class="k">it</span>(<span class="s">'shows the total'</span>, <span class="k">function</span> () &#123;
    <span class="k">expect</span>($this-&gt;get(<span class="s">'/invoices/1001/pdf'</span>))
        -&gt;toHavePdfText(<span class="s">'Invoice 1001'</span>)
        -&gt;toHavePdfText(<span class="s">'120.00'</span>);
&#125;);

<span class="k">it</span>(<span class="s">'matches the approved layout'</span>, <span class="k">function</span> () &#123;
    <span class="k">expect</span>($this-&gt;get(<span class="s">'/invoices/1001/pdf'</span>))
        -&gt;toMatchPdfSnapshot(<span class="s">'invoice-1001'</span>);
&#125;);</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pane pane-term on-ground">
        <div class="pane-inner">
          <p class="pane-title">vendor/bin/pest</p>
          <pre class="terminal" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pest output with one passing and two failing tests"><code>  <span class="badge-fail">FAIL</span> Tests\Feature\InvoicePdfTest
  <span class="pass">✓</span> has one page
  <span class="fail">⨯</span> shows the total
  <span class="fail">⨯</span> matches the approved layout

  <span class="fail">⨯</span> shows the total
  Expected PDF to contain "120.00".
  Extracted text:
  <span class="dim">Invoice 1001  Acme Ltd</span>
  <span class="dim">Design work  100.00</span>
  <span class="dim">VAT  20.00</span>
  <span class="dim">Total</span>

  <span class="fail">⨯</span> matches the approved layout
  PDF snapshot page 1: 312 changed pixels (allowed 0).
  Diff: tests/pdf-snapshots/invoice-1001/artifacts/diff-1.png

  <span class="dim">Tests:</span>  <span class="fail">2 failed</span>, <span class="pass">1 passed</span></code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="checks-section" id="checks" aria-labelledby="checks-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="titled" id="checks-title">Three checks on the real document</h2>
      <dl class="checks">
        <div class="check">
          <dt>toHavePdfText()</dt>
          <dd>Checks for a case-sensitive substring in the PDF's text layer. It does not use OCR or check layout.</dd>
          <dd class="fails">On failure <code>Expected PDF to contain "120.00". Extracted text: …</code></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <dt>toHavePdfPageCount()</dt>
          <dd>Checks the page count, so an unexpected second page fails the test.</dd>
          <dd class="fails">On failure <code>Expected PDF to have 1 page(s); found 2.</code></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <dt>toMatchPdfSnapshot()</dt>
          <dd>Renders each page and compares it with an approved baseline. You can mask one area or allow a set number of changed pixels per page.</dd>
          <dd class="fails">On failure <code>PDF snapshot page 1: 312 changed pixels (allowed 0). Diff: …/diff-1.png</code></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="muted">PHPUnit users can call the same checks as static <code>PdfAssertions</code> methods.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="install on-deep" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="col">
        <p class="eyebrow">Two commands</p>
        <h2 class="titled" id="install-title">Install</h2>
        <p>Add it to an existing Laravel 12 app with Pest or PHPUnit. The second command installs the pinned renderer inside the package. Installation needs network access. Assertions run offline.</p>
        <pre class="terminal" tabindex="0" aria-label="Install commands"><code><span class="dim">$</span> composer require --dev 'craigsimps/laravel-pdf-testing:^0.1' -W
<span class="dim">$</span> vendor/bin/pdf-testing install</code></pre>
        <p class="muted">Existing Pest installations need no registration step. Use your own PDF generator. Full details in the <a href="https://github.com/craigsimps/laravel-pdf-testing#requirements-and-installation">README</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h3>You need</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>PHP 8.3 or 8.4</li>
          <li>Laravel 12 (optional; plain PHPUnit projects work too)</li>
          <li>Pest 3 or PHPUnit 11.5; Pest 4 or PHPUnit 12 (tested on PHP 8.4)</li>
          <li>Node 24.21.0 and npm 11, used only by the renderer</li>
          <li>No browser, Poppler, Ghostscript or hosted service required</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="note"><strong>Offline after install.</strong> Assertions use in-memory PDF data, bundled fonts and a local Node process. No network requests, no telemetry.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="titled" id="demo-title">A complete example</h2>
        <p>A small Laravel app with an invoice PDF route and passing PDF tests. You can clone it and change the invoice to see which tests fail.</p>
        <!-- TODO-DEMO: replace the href with the verified public demo repository URL. -->
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-secondary" id="demo-todo" href="https://github.com/craigsimps/laravel-pdf-testing#demo">Read about the demo</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="col">
        <h3>You control snapshot updates</h3>
        <p>A missing baseline fails. Nothing is created or overwritten unless you ask.</p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li class="step">
            <span class="step-n">01</span>
            <div class="step-body">
              <p><strong>Create the baseline explicitly.</strong></p>
              <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Create a baseline"><code>PDF_TESTING_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 vendor/bin/pest --filter='approved layout'</code></pre>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="step">
            <span class="step-n">02</span>
            <div class="step-body">
              <p><strong>Review the PNGs</strong> in <code>tests/pdf-snapshots/invoice-1001/</code> before you accept them. On a mismatch, <code>artifacts/diff-1.png</code> shows the changed pixels in red.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="step">
            <span class="step-n">03</span>
            <div class="step-body">
              <p><strong>Commit</strong> <code>manifest.json</code> and <code>page-*.png</code>, ignore <code>artifacts/</code>, and never set the update flag in normal CI.</p>
              <p class="muted">Create and compare baselines on the same pinned renderer, operating system and architecture. Snapshots are not portable across operating systems.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="limits-section" id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="intro">
        <h2 class="titled" id="limits-title">Limits</h2>
        <p>Use this for PDFs your app generates. These limits apply to every assertion.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="limits">
        <li><strong>Not OCR.</strong> Scanned PDFs without a text layer, and password-protected PDFs, are out of scope.</li>
        <li><strong>Not a replacement for fakes.</strong> Keep testing that your app requested a PDF. This tests what the PDF contains.</li>
        <li><strong>Not a service.</strong> Everything runs on your machine or CI. The toolkit collects no telemetry.</li>
        <li><strong>Not for untrusted uploads.</strong> It is for your own application and test PDFs, with a 60-second timeout per assertion.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="site-footer on-ground">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p>MIT licensed. Source, changelog and issues on <a href="https://github.com/craigsimps/laravel-pdf-testing">GitHub</a>.</p>
    <p>Laravel is a trademark of Taylor Otwell. This package is independent and not endorsed by Laravel.</p>
  </div>
</footer>

